[{:db/id "q-11974/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "87dbab61-7510-5c79-843e-7b58b2104d25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "281c8f85-07ff-5d78-b469-b69a22a5a942" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8c7837a3-b4d4-51f7-a858-721d1d2c01b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0bed393d-4bcc-521a-8aef-4312269095f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6f7948e4-273d-5c4d-bf11-54a1fbdbd9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9edcd3d5-e0ec-53f8-aac8-7c1370ec12f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11974/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-11974/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-11974/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-11974/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-11974/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-11974/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11974" :question/id #uuid "caa30782-6ec9-52c9-a9a1-a390c30127b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11974" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe quadrilateral $Q$ is mapped to the quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The quadrilateral ${Q}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,-2),(-3,2),(2,2),$ and $(-1,-1).$ Which of the following are vertices of $Q?$\n\n- $(2,2)$\n- $(0,1)$\n- $(-5,-8)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${Q}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $Q$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1-(-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $Q$ are $(0,-2),(-5,-8),(0,2),(0,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-11974/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection/f4d383f82bff7b527921b93b850dbb8a4ec696f737408cb6ab2fb4b502ce71ad" :answer/id #uuid "c2f5be99-d9d7-5b0a-9b95-74b61e556fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection/86c859ea7e7fcde92297612aa8bdceaae9c9d5197ec6f6355cc2681c4f28d257" :answer/id #uuid "8e61e050-d7ea-5983-ad0f-1f81920dd099" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection/a735360462ce4d067fd7726ed9cab8981b173542f41fd1b28580e2de7e57377e" :answer/id #uuid "07d7f9a2-9b6b-5af0-8624-99da4e17ab82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection/007eeed99df76abca20aac14f6ae83d881dea83014f9bc859cc358ed08ef95fe" :answer/id #uuid "b2ddba95-46f8-5fc8-bf97-b845f28b2622" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection/e042245db05905a49c7bbef958a3a25ae63cdcdd5e73bbff5f71cb53b87e3e87" :answer/id #uuid "74ac71aa-9b2e-5d56-bc4c-2eb6f662df32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b50b5c-7956-5979-9252-0e141fbd3028" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85082/selection/a735360462ce4d067fd7726ed9cab8981b173542f41fd1b28580e2de7e57377e" :answer-field/choices ["q-85082/selection/f4d383f82bff7b527921b93b850dbb8a4ec696f737408cb6ab2fb4b502ce71ad" "q-85082/selection/86c859ea7e7fcde92297612aa8bdceaae9c9d5197ec6f6355cc2681c4f28d257" "q-85082/selection/a735360462ce4d067fd7726ed9cab8981b173542f41fd1b28580e2de7e57377e" "q-85082/selection/007eeed99df76abca20aac14f6ae83d881dea83014f9bc859cc358ed08ef95fe" "q-85082/selection/e042245db05905a49c7bbef958a3a25ae63cdcdd5e73bbff5f71cb53b87e3e87"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85082" :question/id #uuid "612312a8-5a63-51fc-aaa1-05ecae9204ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-85082" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{18-16}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-85082/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85082"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9c27db8b-aedb-53fc-81e0-2a26e5c66a1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186283844 :answer-field/choices ["q-317436/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317512/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "9cc78149-c373-5a4d-9532-ecfd86aa4a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317512/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6099022-befe-5030-a967-074c59118117" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317512/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-317512/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317512/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "888bc2d2-9e81-5d58-8d0b-18ed53aa14ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317512/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e26931db-9080-575c-aa98-70707f72bb2f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317512/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-317512/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317512" :question/id #uuid "c958b406-f3a4-5d32-8a33-a3b0b332da95" :question/math-academy-id "q-317512" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(1)(-3)-(2)(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3+2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317512/field-1" "q-317512/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317512"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
